"""
Seed data for the Math Proficiency Assessment question bank.

IMPORTANT -- this file is NOT the runtime source of questions anymore.
At runtime, questions live in the Postgres `questions` table (see
`models.py`). This file only supplies the initial/default content: on
first startup (or when running `scripts/seed_db.py` directly), the app
checks whether the `questions` table is empty and, if so, loads the rows
below into it. Once seeded, editing this file has no effect unless you
re-run the seed script against an empty table (or edit the DB directly /
via a future admin UI).

Grade range: Kindergarten through Grade 6. Kindergarten is represented
as grade 0 (the `grade` column is an Integer) so no schema change was
needed to add it -- see `scoring.grade_label()` / the frontend's
`lib/gradeLabel.ts` for the 0 -> "K" display mapping used everywhere a
grade number is shown to a user.

SCALE: 753 questions total across 36 distinct math topics (concepts) --
every single topic has AT LEAST 20 questions, so there's real depth to
sample from no matter which concept a child ends up being tested on
repeatedly. A child only ever answers 20 questions in one sitting (see
QUESTIONS_TOTAL_PER_ATTEMPT in main.py), drawn as a stratified sample
across all 7 grade levels -- NOT the whole pool. `GET /api/questions`
does this sampling (see `repository.get_sampled_questions()`), and when
called with a `kid_id`, draws preferentially from questions that
specific kid hasn't been asked before, so different kids -- and the same
kid on a retake -- see different questions rather than the same fixed
set every time. See the "Question sampling" section of README.md for
the full rationale and how this was verified against a live database.

This file's 753 questions were generated programmatically by
`scripts/generate_questions.py` (fixed random seed, so re-running it
reproduces the same set -- pass --seed for a different one), with every
correct answer computed directly from the same arithmetic the question
describes, and independently spot-checked afterward by re-parsing a
sample of the generated question text and recomputing the answer from
scratch (213 questions checked this way, zero discrepancies). Two
content-ambiguity bugs were found and fixed during generation -- e.g. an
earlier "which shape has 4 sides?" question could have both "Square" and
"Rectangle" as options, which is genuinely ambiguous since both have 4
sides -- see the generator script's comments for the fix (same-property
shapes are now excluded from co-occurring as options).

Each question is tagged with a `grade` (0-6) representing the grade
level the skill is typically taught at, and a `topic` for reporting
purposes.

`options` is always a list of 4 possible answers.
`correct_index` is the 0-based index into `options` of the correct answer.

`visual` is an OPTIONAL diagram spec consumed by the frontend's VisualAid
component when the student turns on "visual aids" mode. It never reveals
the answer -- it only illustrates the numbers/operation in the question.
Not every question has one (some topics -- e.g. Statistics, Coordinate
Plane, Patterns -- don't map cleanly onto any of the existing diagram
types; see README.md for which visual types exist).
Supported `type` values and their params (all rendered as SVG on the
frontend, see frontend/components/VisualAid.tsx):

  number_line   { min, max, step, marks:[{value,label}], jump?:{from,to,label} }
  base10        { operator:"+"|"-", a:{tens,ones,label}, b:{tens,ones,label} }
  place_value   { number, highlight: "ones"|"tens"|"hundreds"|"thousands" }
  array_grid    { rows, cols, label }
  groups        { groupCount, itemsPerGroup, itemLabel }
  area_model    { widthParts:[..], heightParts:[..], label? }
  fraction_bars { bars:[{numerator, denominator, label}] }  (numerator may be null = unshaded)
  decimal_area  { a, b }   -- 10x10 grid showing a * b as overlapping shaded regions
  percent_grid  { shaded, label }
  ratio_blocks  { ratioA, ratioB, labelA, labelB, multiplier }
  tape_diagram  { segments:[{label, repeatCount, color, isConstant}], total }
  algebra_tiles { terms:[{coeff, isConstant}] }
  expression_steps { expression, highlight }
  exponent_tower { base, exponent }
  triangle_squares { legA, legB }
  shape_row     { shapes:[{name}] }  -- shows each named basic shape in a row with its
                                          label, for pre-readers matching a shape word
                                          to its picture. Never highlights/orders toward
                                          the correct answer.
  compare_groups { groupA:{count,label}, groupB:{count,label} }  -- two labeled groups
                                          of dots side by side, for "which is more" or
                                          simple "combine two groups" word problems.

IMPORTANT: the correct_index in this file (and in the DB) is never sent
to the frontend -- the API layer strips it before returning questions.
"""

from typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, TypedDict


class SeedQuestion(TypedDict):
    id: int
    grade: int
    topic: str
    question: str
    options: List[str]
    correct_index: int
    visual: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]


